  "limitations": [
    "The workshop is far heavier than the small spacecraft these NASA surveys cover, and would need many more engines.",
    "The electric route uses the same speed change as two short burns. A real low-thrust spiral needs more, so its time is a best case.",
    "Changing orbital plane costs nothing here, though a real return would pay for it.",
    "Burns by the chemical engine are treated as instant.",
    "Eclipses, radiation exposure, and the wait to reach the top of the orbit are left out.",
    "The fictional values were chosen to create this trade-off, and small changes would flip some results."
  ]
